  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Doraemon has a matrix with NNN rows (numbered 111 through NNN) and MMM columns (numbered 111 through MMM). Let's denote the element in row iii and column jjj by Ai,jA_{i,j}Ai,j​. Next, let's define a sub-row of a row rrr as a sequence Ar,x,Ar,x+1,…,Ar,yA_{r, x}, A_{r, x+1}, \\ldots, A_{r, y}Ar,x​,Ar,x+1​,…,Ar,y​ for some xxx and yyy (1≤x≤y≤M1 \\le x \\le y \\le M1≤x≤y≤M) and a sub-column of a column ccc by Ax,c,Ax+1,c,…,Ay,cA_{x, c}, A_{x+1, c}, \\ldots, A_{y, c}Ax,c​,Ax+1,c​,…,Ay,c​ for some xxx and yyy (1≤x≤y≤N1 \\le x \\le y \\le N1≤x≤y≤N).\n\nYou need to find the number of pairs (sub-row of some row, sub-column of some column) with the following properties:\n\n\nBoth sequences (the sub-row and the sub-column) have the same length.\nThis length is odd.\nThe central elements of both sequences are the same (they correspond to the same element of the matrix).\nBoth sequences are palindromes.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N,M1 \\le N, M1≤N,M",
      "N⋅M≤105N \\cdot M \\le 10^5N⋅M≤105",
      "1≤Ai,j≤1061 \\le A_{i, j} \\le 10^61≤Ai,j​≤106 for each valid i,ji, ji,j",
      "the sum of N⋅MN \\cdot MN⋅M over all test cases does not exceed 3⋅1053 \\cdot 10^53⋅105",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (30 points):**",
      "T≤10T \\le 10T≤10",
      "N⋅M≤103N \\cdot M \\le 10^3N⋅M≤103"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and MMM.\nNNN lines follow. For each iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N), the iii-th of these lines contains MMM space-separated integers Ai,1,Ai,2,…,Ai,MA_{i, 1}, A_{i, 2}, \\ldots, A_{i, M}Ai,1​,Ai,2​,…,Ai,M​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer ― the number of valid pairs.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
